  /// unique identifier is the function name with a function version or alias
  /// name suffix that is not $LATEST . Example: function:my-function:prod or
  /// function:my-function:1 . Amazon Keyspaces table - The resource type is
  /// table and the unique identifier is the table name. Example:
  /// keyspace/mykeyspace/table/mytable . Amazon MSK cluster - The resource
  /// type and unique identifier are specified using the cluster ARN. Example:
  /// arn:aws:kafka:us-east-1:123456789012:cluster/demo-cluster-1/6357e0b2-0e6a-4b86-a0b4-70df934c2e31-5
  /// . Amazon ElastiCache replication group - The resource type is
